              "inline_data": null,
              "text": "Depending on whether you are looking for a **button-down** utility shirt or a **long-sleeve t-shirt/hoodie** (sun shirt), the thin PFG (Performance Fishing Gear) shirts from Columbia are called:\n\n### 1. The Button-Down Style: **The PFG Tamiami (or Tamiami II)**\nIf you are looking for the classic collared button-up shirt with chest pockets, you are likely thinking of the **Tamiami**. \n* **The Fabric:** It is made of 100% polyester ripstop, which makes it **extremely thin, silky, and feather-light**. \n* **How it compares:** Many people confuse it with the classic Columbia **Bahama** shirt. While the Bahama is made of a stiffer, heavier nylon, the Tamiami is specifically designed to be the thinnest, most breathable, and most comfortable button-down they offer in hot weather.\n\n### 2. The T-Shirt / Hoodie Style: **The PFG Terminal Tackle**\nIf you are thinking of the smooth, stretchy long-sleeve shirt (with or without a hood) that looks like athletic wear, it is called the **Terminal Tackle**.\n* **The Fabric:** It is a very thin, lightweight, and smooth 100% polyester interlock shirt.\n* **What it\u2019s for:** Often referred to as a **\"sun shirt,\" \"sun hoodie,\"** or **\"rash guard,\"** it features Omni-Shade UPF 50 sun protection and Omni-Wick moisture-wicking technology. It is designed to be worn in the blazing heat (or even in the water) to keep you cool and protected without having to wear sunscreen. \n\n**Summary:** Ask for the **Tamiami** if you want a thin button-down, or the **Terminal Tackle** if you want a thin long-sleeve tee.",
